\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:42:52-08:00","id":69377,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Exigents will have room for that kind of thing, I'm with Sage in that there's a lot of room to cover and I've got no idea how to let this pass by the gaze of the Dread God Wordcount unscathed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:48:37-08:00","id":69387,"title":"","content":"I also think that it's far enough into house rules territory that &quot;what ever works for your game&quot; is probably good enough. I know that I plan on making at least 2-3 different types of exalts for my own games and at least one of them will probably have a sub-system, so I would really like some guidelines, but I would rather have a strong basis and plenty of examples for designing charms. (If I had to choose)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:54:25-08:00","id":69396,"ti